    Fix React error #310: restore full SalesRepPortal.tsx from initial commit and move hooks before early returns
    
    Root cause: The file was truncated to 590 lines (down from 1522) in commit ba25463,
    replacing the full JSX with 'return null;' placeholder. The truncation broke the
    component AND hid the real bug: useCreateCustomer() and useMutation() were declared
    AFTER 4 conditional early-return statements (if (!reps), if (!selectedRepId), etc.).
    
    On first render, reps is undefined -> early return -> 33 hooks called.
    On second render, reps loads -> 35 hooks called -> React error #310.
    
    Fix: Restored the original 1522-line file from commit 92d5ff3, then moved both
    hook declarations (useCreateCustomer, useMutation) from after the early returns
    to before them (lines 279-367). All 35 hooks now run unconditionally on every
    render with a consistent order, regardless of which early-return guard fires.

